{"kind":"request","text":"A pure predict for optimistic interfaces.\n\nGive clients a pure `predict` that judges a proposed intent against the local fold with the same derive functions the scope uses, so an interface can show the result before the receipt arrives and reconcile when it does.\n\nSource: Hugh's request of 28 October 2026, after a review of the alchemy Domain package, which offers an aggregate predict and a view evolve for optimistic interfaces. In dap the judges are already pure and shared with replay, so this is client work, not kernel work. The planner may attach this to an existing work item or sequence it.\n\nToday: the browser and the card views wait for the accepted answer. The offline and sync note (notes/2026-10-09-offline-and-sync-design.md) designs a signed local outbox and reconciliation, and nothing in it is built. `followReceipt` checks an accepted receipt against the entry.\n\nWanted:\n1. `predict(fold, definition, signedIntent, now)` in `@generalbusiness/dap-client`: runs the judge and the fold over the client's local copy, with a stated clock, and returns the predicted entry and the predicted fold, or the refusal the judges would give. It evaluates rule expressions locally. It cannot read grants, facts of other scopes or capability answers; for an act that needs one it returns `undecidable` and names what it would need.\n2. The declared view projections (`window.dapSurface`) accept a predicted entry as a pending overlay, marked as such, replace it when the receipt's entry arrives, and drop it on refusal.\n3. A witness that for every scenario of the lending library the prediction equals the scope's entry byte for byte when the act is accepted, and names the same reason when it is refused.\n4. The offline note is updated to rest its local outbox on this function.","body":{"conditions":"Landed on main with the predict function, the pending overlay in the card views, the lending witness and the offline note update; or superseded by a planner act naming the request that carries this work.","target_head":"0881c1bca1df31a9fdb4ae72947cbbedf1b3ec51","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}